  "reason": "The current best is config_038 (0.7207 acc) using scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + concat. The only untested dimension within this exact configuration family is the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted). Config_039 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted, isolating that single variable. This is the highest-value next test because: (1) it directly probes whether a learned weighting of modalities can outperform simple concatenation, potentially pushing accuracy above 0.72; (2) it requires only one change from the known best, avoiding confounds; (3) with only 2 experiments remaining, confirming or rejecting the current fusion choice lets the final experiments either exploit a new best or pivot to another axis (e.g., aggregation or image encoder). RNA-only evidence (transformer ≈ avgpool) suggests aggregation is not the bottleneck, making fusion the most promising untested lever."
